# RTU API is read-only

Call the RTU SOAP API only to read. A write is allowed only when a separate task names that exact operation. Settings, an access check, a bugfix, or write bits on the role do not allow a write.

`POST` is the SOAP transport. It is not a mutation. This service may send these reads:

- `getObjects` (`table` and `procedure`) from Settings → «Проверить доступ».
- `describeTable` and `selectRowset` from «Текущие звонки» for «Транзитные вызовы (ПКомм)» and «Транзитные вызовы (ПУпр)»: the summary pages, or, when those are absent, the shared templates «Конференции Class 4» and «Вызовы» plus «Активные модули». Limit 2000. Offset is 0, 2000, 4000, 6000, or 8000. Filter and sort are nil. A `node` header is sent only on `selectRowset`, and only for a `signaling-<digits>` or `scripting-<digits>` module, at most four of each.
- `describeTable` and `selectRowset` from `groups.sync` for the page «Входящие группы» in the folder «Оборудование». The same limit and offsets. Filter and sort are nil. No `node` header. No `getLookup`. A complete list, including an empty one, replaces `routing_groups`.
- `describeTable` and `selectRowset` from `phones.sync` for the page «Оборудование» in the folder «Оборудование». Limit 2000. Offset is 0, 2000, and so on, at most 25 pages, so the last offset is 48000. Filter and sort are nil. No `node` header. `getLookup` or `getColumnLookup` only for «Тип оборудования», «Протокол сигнализации», and «Входящие группы», and only when `describeTable` sets `have_lookup`. `getColumnLookup` is sent only when that operation is in the fetched WSDL v2. When neither operation is there, one `getLookup` uses the accepted `describeTable` style. A missing lookup fails that job. `countRowset` is one nil-filter count of that same page, and only when the fetched WSDL v2 contains that operation with `p_table_hi` and `p_filter`. A complete read replaces `phone_endpoints` and `phone_gateways` only when the row count matches and the snapshot still has the previous side, passwords, zones, protocols, address lists, and groups. An empty page does not wipe a non-empty catalog.
- `getLookup` for the technical name of «Состояние вызова» on the ПУпр table already selected above, and only when `describeTable` sets `have_lookup` on that column. No `node` header. One success stays until the catalog is dropped. A failure retries at most once a minute and does not fail the call snapshot.
- `describeTable` and `selectRowset` from `regs.poll` for «Регистрации (ПКомм)» and «Регистрации (ПУпр)». A summary page under «Мониторинг ПКомм» and outside «Данные по модулям» is one `selectRowset` with no `node` header. When that page is absent, the shared template whose leaf is «Регистрации» is read instead, plus «Активные модули». `node` is then sent only on those registration `selectRowset` calls: `signaling-<digits>` for ПКомм and `scripting-<digits>` for ПУпр, at most four of each. A named module copy is not a source. The same limit and offsets. Filter and sort are nil. `getLookup` only for «Состояние» on the ПКомм page, and only when `describeTable` sets `have_lookup` on that column. `getColumnLookup` is sent only when that operation is in the fetched WSDL v2, for the same column and without `node`. When neither operation is there, one `getLookup` uses the accepted `describeTable` style. A missing or unread lookup does not fail the job. An unrecognized state does. «Время окончания регистрации» is added to the same ПКомм `selectRowset` only when that title occurs once and the technical name is acceptable. It is not looked up, and its absence does not fail the read. A complete non-empty list replaces `reg_current` and adds catalog numbers whose «Регистрация» is «Да» and that are missing from the page. An empty page does not wipe a non-empty `reg_current`.

Do not add `getLookup` for any other column. Do not add `getObjectId`, `describeObject`, `describeProcedure`, `describeProcedureContext`, or `countRowset` for any other page. Do not point `describeTable` or `selectRowset` at any other object.

Do not send `insertRowset`, `updateRowset`, `deleteRowset`, `transaction`, `checkRowset`, `call`, `callContext`, API v1 except `getColumnLookup` when the fetched WSDL v2 contains that operation, the `args:node` header except on the `selectRowset` calls named above, or the `http://mfisoft.ru/auth` namespace. `checkRowset` is a write: its actions are `insert`, `update`, and `delete`.

The operation name is a literal in the envelope builder: `getObjects`, `describeTable`, `selectRowset`, `countRowset`, `getLookup`, or `getColumnLookup`. Do not accept an operation name from a caller, a flag, or the WSDL. Ignore write operations that appear in the WSDL.

Do not invent object names. Do not send headers or bodies that are not in the 2.0 handbook or the live WSDL v2. Do not log the SOAP envelope. The password stays ciphertext at rest and is sent only on the pinned HTTPS host.
